-- Focus follows the mouse ONLY on click, never on hover (user directive).
-- `input:follow_mouse = 0` — Hyprland wiki (configuring/variables): "cursor
-- focus will be detached from keyboard focus completely. Clicking on a
-- window will move keyboard focus to that window", hovering will not. This
-- is a config VARIABLE, not a dispatch, so it survives `hyprctl reload` —
-- a one-shot `hyprctl keyword` inside an `hyprland.start` hook would not
-- (that event does not refire on reload, see the AUTOSTART note below).
--
-- The nested-table `hl.config({ input = { ... } })` form is confirmed
-- against hyprwm/Hyprland's own example/hyprland.lua, which sets
-- `follow_mouse` in exactly this shape. This is the first `hl.config` call
-- in this file — everything else so far has run on Hyprland's own defaults.
hl.config({
    input = {
        follow_mouse = 0,
    },
})

