-- docs/TODO.md: "the mouse cursor often disappear arbitrarily." Root cause,
-- read from Hyprland's own source of truth for its defaults (hyprwm/
-- hyprland-wiki, configuring/core/config-options.md, `cursor` category,
-- fetched this session rather than assumed): `cursor:hide_on_touch`
-- defaults to `true` ("Hides the cursor when the last input was a touch
-- input until a mouse input is done") — nothing in this file ever set it,
-- so Hyprland's own untouched default was in effect the whole time. razer
-- has a touchscreen (capabilities doc, PHI_CAP_TOUCHSCREEN; the GESTURES
-- section's own three-finger-swipe comment further down: "razer has both"
-- a touchpad and a touchscreen firing through the same gesture engine) —
-- any touch contact with the screen, deliberate or an incidental brush
-- while adjusting the lid, silently hides the pointer until the next
-- mouse-classified input, which reads exactly as "arbitrary." zotac has no
-- touchscreen (mini never renders this template at all — headless, no
-- graphical session), so this is a no-op there — same reasoning as the
-- GESTURES section's touchscreen swipe binds ("simply inert", no host
-- guard needed).
--
-- No `pcall` needed here, unlike the GESTURES block below (C-06: a raised
-- Lua error discards the WHOLE reload): confirmed against the real
-- hyprwm/Hyprland source (`src/config/lua/ConfigManager.cpp`,
-- `CConfigManager::CConfigManager()`) that `hl.config` registers every
-- entry of `Values::CONFIG_VALUES` — the same master keyword registry the
-- plain-`.conf` parser uses — generically, with no category whitelist.
-- `cursor:hide_on_touch` is a real entry in that registry (same source as
-- above), not a guessed category name.
hl.config({
    cursor = {
        hide_on_touch = false,
    },
})

